{"id": "toolu_01KMHAeU95qriduzhvoe1fju", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"code": "open('notes.md','a').write(\"\"\"\n## Findings (session 1)\n- mean_hidden = masked mean over ALL tokens incl CLS/SEP (matches uniform attention).\n- Base features: feats.npz (M0..M12 mean, C0..C12 cls, y), folds.npy (5-fold stratified). passes 2-3.\n- CV ridge (stdz): single-layer mean ~95.6-96.5%; CLS worse. Concat shallow+deep helps: [M0,M11] 97.5, [M4,M11] 97.4, [M6,M11] 97.4, [C11,M11] 96.8.\n- M0 NOT linearly recoverable from M11 (sentence R2 .55, token-level R2 .38). No inert residual subspace (QKV min sv ~1/3 median).\n- Attention to CLS from other tokens (pass 6): enc layers 1-3 high (20-35%), layers 4-11 low (2-5%).\n- Token states for 128 texts at L0/6/11: tok128.npz (passes 4-5).\n## Exact readout design (layer 11, only CLS output matters)\n- head0 uniform (Wq=0,bq=0), value rows0..7 = A (8x768), bias b -> CLS gets A\u00b7M11+b. O writes c*(.) into 8 channel dims ch, other heads V=0.\n- LN1 gamma=1,beta=0; FFN W2=0,b2=0; LN2 gamma=1,beta=0 -> final CLS = LN(h11_cls + c*chan).\n- pooler row k = s*(B_k on non-ch dims (B_k summed=0) + e_ch[k]/c); classifier = I. => argmax(B h11cls + A M11 + b) exactly.\n- Plan: first implement with base C11/M11 (target ~96.8%), then try a layer-6 'CLS tap' (rank-1 W_q fix making CLS attention ~uniform) to inject M6 into CLS.\n\"\"\")\nF=np.load('feats.npz'); y=F['y']; folds=np.load('folds.npy')\nC=F['C11']; M=F['M11']\n# choose channel dims: lowest variance dims of C11\nv=C.var(0); ch=np.argsort(v)[:8]; print('channel dims',ch, v[ch].round(4), 'median var',np.median(v).round(3))\nkeep=np.setdiff1d(np.arange(768),ch)\ndef stdz(X,tr): mu=X[tr].mean(0); sd=X[tr].std(0)+1e-6; return (X-mu)/sd\ndef cv(featfn, lam):\n    accs=[]\n    for f in range(5):\n        tr=folds!=f; te=~tr\n        Z=featfn(tr); mu=Z[tr].mean(0); Zc=Z-mu\n        Y=np.eye(8)[y[tr]]-1/8\n        K=Zc@Zc[tr].T; a=np.linalg.solve(K[tr]+lam*np.eye(tr.sum()),Y); pr=K[te]@a\n        accs.append((np.argmax(pr,1)==y[te]).mean())\n    return round(np.mean(accs),4)\nCc=C[:,keep]-C[:,keep].mean(1,keepdims=True)\nfor wc in [0.5,0.7,1.0]:\n    fn=lambda tr: np.concatenate([wc*stdz(Cc,tr),stdz(M,tr)],1)\n    print('wc',wc,[cv(fn,l) for l in [100,200,300,500,800]])"}, "name": "run_python", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}
